IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `scr-dates`
IMPORT `scr-judgment`

-- Supreme Court (General Civil Procedure) Rules 2025 (Vic) -- worked cases for the party's questions about default and
-- summary judgment, dismissal, discontinuance and offers of compromise (scr-judgment.l4). Every expected value was worked
-- by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the
-- ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are illustrative.
-- Calendar used: 2 November 2026 is a Monday; 1 December 2026 a Tuesday; 1 January 2027 a Friday. The Christmas vacation
-- (24 December to 9 January) is 17 days.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`

§§ `Order 21 -- default judgment`

-- Arguments: writ, default, affidavit filed, statement of claim, Commercial List, defendant under disability without
-- guardian, claim, Australian dollars.
-- An injury claim, no appearance: interlocutory judgment for damages to be assessed.
#ASSERT `What judgment can I get by default` TRUE `no appearance filed within the time` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `damages` TRUE EQUALS JUST `interlocutory judgment for damages to be assessed, with costs`
#ASSERT `What judgment can I get by default` TRUE `no defence served within the time` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `damages` TRUE EQUALS JUST `interlocutory judgment for damages to be assessed, with costs`
#ASSERT `What judgment can I get by default` TRUE `the defence was struck out` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `damages` TRUE EQUALS JUST `interlocutory judgment for damages to be assessed, with costs`
#ASSERT `What judgment can I get by default` TRUE `no appearance filed within the time` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `a debt` TRUE EQUALS JUST `final judgment for the debt, with interest and costs`
#ASSERT `What judgment can I get by default` TRUE `no appearance filed within the time` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `the recovery of land` TRUE EQUALS JUST `judgment for possession of the land, with costs`
#ASSERT `What judgment can I get by default` TRUE `no appearance filed within the time` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `the detention of goods` TRUE EQUALS JUST `interlocutory judgment for the goods or their value to be assessed, with costs`
#ASSERT `What judgment can I get by default` TRUE `no appearance filed within the time` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `other relief` TRUE EQUALS JUST `the Court may give judgment on the statement of claim`
#ASSERT `What judgment can I get by default` TRUE `no appearance filed within the time` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `other relief` TRUE EQUALS JUST `no default judgment yet`
-- Damages in a foreign currency: the Court under r 21.04, needing a statement of claim (r 21.03(1.2)).
#ASSERT `What judgment can I get by default` TRUE `no appearance filed within the time` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `damages` FALSE EQUALS JUST `the Court may give judgment on the statement of claim`
#ASSERT `What judgment can I get by default` TRUE `no appearance filed within the time` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `damages` FALSE EQUALS JUST `no default judgment yet`
-- No affidavit; a Commercial List Judge; a defendant under disability with no guardian.
#ASSERT `What judgment can I get by default` TRUE `no appearance filed within the time` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `damages` TRUE EQUALS JUST `no default judgment yet`
#ASSERT `What judgment can I get by default` TRUE `no appearance filed within the time` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `damages` TRUE EQUALS JUST `no default judgment yet`
#ASSERT `What judgment can I get by default` TRUE `no appearance filed within the time` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE `damages` TRUE EQUALS JUST `no default judgment yet`
#ASSERT `What judgment can I get by default` TRUE `no default` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `damages` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What judgment can I get by default` FALSE `no appearance filed within the time` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `damages` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Order 22 -- summary judgment times`

-- Hearing Monday 30 November 2026: 14 days back, Monday 16 November. Hearing Monday 18 January 2027: 17 to 10 January
-- (8), then 23 to 18 December (6): Friday 18 December 2026. Hearing Wednesday 13 January 2027: 12 to 10 January (3), then
-- 23 to 13 December (11): Sunday 13 December, moved to Monday 14 December (fork F10).
#ASSERT `By when must my summary judgment application be served` (`d` 30 11 2026) EQUALS `d` 16 11 2026
#ASSERT `By when must my summary judgment application be served` (`d` 18 1 2027) EQUALS `d` 18 12 2026
#ASSERT `By when must my summary judgment application be served` (`d` 13 1 2027) EQUALS `d` 14 12 2026

-- Three days back, weekends not counted: hearing Monday 16 November, Wednesday 11; hearing Thursday 19 November, Monday 16.
#ASSERT `By when must my affidavit against summary judgment be served` (`d` 16 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (`d` 11 11 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must my affidavit against summary judgment be served` (`d` 19 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (`d` 16 11 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must my affidavit against summary judgment be served` (`d` 19 11 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `Can the summary judgment against me be set aside` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the summary judgment against me be set aside` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Order 24`

#ASSERT `Can my proceeding be dismissed for want of prosecution` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my proceeding be dismissed for want of prosecution` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my proceeding be dismissed for want of prosecution` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my proceeding be dismissed for want of prosecution` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `What can follow my failure to obey the order` `plaintiff` TRUE EQUALS JUST `my proceeding may be dismissed`
#ASSERT `What can follow my failure to obey the order` `defendant` TRUE EQUALS JUST `my defence may be struck out, and judgment in default of defence may follow`
#ASSERT `What can follow my failure to obey the order` `plaintiff` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Arguments: dismissed or discontinued, owes costs, paid, same cause.
#ASSERT `Can my new case be stayed until I pay the old costs` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my new case be stayed until I pay the old costs` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my new case be stayed until I pay the old costs` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my new case be stayed until I pay the old costs` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Order 25`

-- Arguments: writ, pleadings closed, all consent.
#ASSERT `May I discontinue without leave` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I discontinue without leave` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May I discontinue without leave` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I discontinue without leave` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May I discontinue without leave` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `Must I pay costs if I discontinue` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I pay costs if I discontinue` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my discontinuance a defence to a new case` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my discontinuance a defence to a new case` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Arguments: last step, r 3.06 notice, Prothonotary sent, day sent, notice of intention filed, day filed, today.
-- Last step 1 March 2025: the year (with 17 vacation days) ends 18 March 2026.
#ASSERT `What happens to my inactive case now` (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) (`d` 18 3 2026) EQUALS `not yet open to a dismissal notice`
#ASSERT `What happens to my inactive case now` (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) (`d` 19 3 2026) EQUALS `open to a dismissal notice from the Prothonotary`
#ASSERT `What happens to my inactive case now` (`d` 1 3 2025) TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) (`d` 19 3 2027) EQUALS `not yet open to a dismissal notice`
-- Notice sent Monday 2 November 2026: 30 days, Wednesday 2 December.
#ASSERT `What happens to my inactive case now` (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE TRUE (`d` 2 11 2026) TRUE (`d` 2 12 2026) (`d` 9 12 2026) EQUALS `kept alive by a notice of intention to continue`
#ASSERT `What happens to my inactive case now` (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE TRUE (`d` 2 11 2026) TRUE (`d` 3 12 2026) (`d` 9 12 2026) EQUALS `dismissed without adjudication on the merits`
#ASSERT `What happens to my inactive case now` (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE TRUE (`d` 2 11 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) (`d` 2 12 2026) EQUALS `a party may still file a notice of intention to continue`
#ASSERT `What happens to my inactive case now` (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE TRUE (`d` 2 11 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) (`d` 3 12 2026) EQUALS `dismissed without adjudication on the merits`

-- Sent 2 November 2026: 2 December. Sent Friday 27 November 2026: 28 November to 23 December (26), then 10 to 13 January
-- (4): Wednesday 13 January 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must the notice of intention to continue be filed` (`d` 2 11 2026) EQUALS `d` 2 12 2026
#ASSERT `By when must the notice of intention to continue be filed` (`d` 27 11 2026) EQUALS `d` 13 1 2027

§§ `Order 26 -- offers of compromise`

-- Arguments: writing in form, says Order 26, says costs, limited in time, days.
#ASSERT `Is my offer of compromise in proper form` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my offer of compromise in proper form` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 14 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my offer of compromise in proper form` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 13 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my offer of compromise in proper form` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my offer of compromise in proper form` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Arguments: served, states a time, days, verdict, day of verdict, public holiday.
-- Served Monday 2 November 2026, no time stated: 14 days, Monday 16 November; 21 days stated: Monday 23 November; 7 days
-- stated: read as 14 (fork F12).
#ASSERT `Until when can I accept the offer` (`d` 2 11 2026) FALSE 0 FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS `d` 16 11 2026
#ASSERT `Until when can I accept the offer` (`d` 2 11 2026) TRUE 21 FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS `d` 23 11 2026
#ASSERT `Until when can I accept the offer` (`d` 2 11 2026) TRUE 7 FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS `d` 16 11 2026
#ASSERT `Until when can I accept the offer` (`d` 2 11 2026) FALSE 0 FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) TRUE EQUALS `d` 17 11 2026
-- A verdict on 10 November comes sooner: the day before it (fork F13); a verdict on 17 November is later than the 16th.
#ASSERT `Until when can I accept the offer` (`d` 2 11 2026) FALSE 0 TRUE (`d` 10 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS `d` 9 11 2026
#ASSERT `Until when can I accept the offer` (`d` 2 11 2026) FALSE 0 TRUE (`d` 17 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS `d` 16 11 2026
-- Served Thursday 10 December 2026: 11 to 23 December (13), then 10 January (14th): Sunday, so Monday 11 January 2027.
#ASSERT `Until when can I accept the offer` (`d` 10 12 2026) FALSE 0 FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS `d` 11 1 2027

#ASSERT `Can I still accept the offer` (`d` 2 11 2026) FALSE 0 FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) (`d` 16 11 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I still accept the offer` (`d` 2 11 2026) FALSE 0 FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) (`d` 17 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I still accept the offer` (`d` 2 11 2026) FALSE 0 TRUE (`d` 10 11 2026) (`d` 10 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Accepted Monday 2 November 2026: 28 days, Monday 30 November. Accepted Tuesday 1 December 2026: 2 to 23 December (22),
-- then 10 to 15 January (6): Friday 15 January 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must the accepted sum be paid` (`d` 2 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (`d` 30 11 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must the accepted sum be paid` (`d` 1 12 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (`d` 15 1 2027)
#ASSERT `By when must the accepted sum be paid` (`d` 2 11 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `May I withdraw my acceptance` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I withdraw my acceptance` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May I withdraw my acceptance` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Arguments: defaulted, joint defendants, contribution rights, offer against all.
#ASSERT `Can I apply to enforce the accepted offer` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I apply to enforce the accepted offer` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I apply to enforce the accepted offer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I apply to enforce the accepted offer` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I apply to enforce the accepted offer` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `May my offer be mentioned to the trial judge` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May my offer be mentioned to the trial judge` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May my offer be mentioned to the trial judge` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- r 26.08. Arguments: who, accepted, injury claim, amount offered, plaintiff judgment, judgment amount, post-offer
-- interest, unreasonable, willing and able, only liability, genuine, Court otherwise.
-- A plaintiff's $300,000 offer in an injury claim; judgment $320,000 with $10,000 post-offer interest: $310,000, no less
-- favourable: indemnity costs.
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the unaccepted offer` `the plaintiff` FALSE TRUE 300000 TRUE 320000 10000 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the plaintiff's costs on the indemnity basis`
-- Judgment $305,000 with $10,000 post-offer interest: $295,000, less favourable: no r 26.08 order.
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the unaccepted offer` `the plaintiff` FALSE TRUE 300000 TRUE 305000 10000 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no costs order under rule 26.08`
-- Exactly the offer: "no less favourable".
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the unaccepted offer` `the plaintiff` FALSE TRUE 300000 TRUE 300000 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the plaintiff's costs on the indemnity basis`
-- Not an injury claim.
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the unaccepted offer` `the plaintiff` FALSE FALSE 300000 TRUE 320000 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the plaintiff's costs on the standard basis to 11 am on the second business day after service, and on the indemnity basis after`
-- Only liability in dispute: needs a genuine compromise (r 26.08(8)).
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the unaccepted offer` `the plaintiff` FALSE TRUE 300000 TRUE 300000 0 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no costs order under rule 26.08`
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the unaccepted offer` `the plaintiff` FALSE TRUE 300000 TRUE 300000 0 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the plaintiff's costs on the indemnity basis`
-- Not willing and able (r 26.08(7)); the Court otherwise; the offer accepted.
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the unaccepted offer` `the plaintiff` FALSE TRUE 300000 TRUE 320000 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no costs order under rule 26.08`
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the unaccepted offer` `the plaintiff` FALSE TRUE 300000 TRUE 320000 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no costs order under rule 26.08`
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the unaccepted offer` `the plaintiff` TRUE TRUE 300000 TRUE 320000 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no costs order under rule 26.08`
-- The plaintiff lost after its own offer.
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the unaccepted offer` `the plaintiff` FALSE TRUE 300000 FALSE 0 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no costs order under rule 26.08`
-- A defendant's $200,000 offer: judgment $180,000, $200,000 (not more favourable), $200,001 (more favourable), and
-- $210,000 with $15,000 post-offer interest ($195,000).
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the unaccepted offer` `the defendant` FALSE TRUE 200000 TRUE 180000 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the plaintiff's costs on the standard basis to 11 am on the second business day after service, and the defendant's costs on the standard basis after`
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the unaccepted offer` `the defendant` FALSE TRUE 200000 TRUE 200000 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the plaintiff's costs on the standard basis to 11 am on the second business day after service, and the defendant's costs on the standard basis after`
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the unaccepted offer` `the defendant` FALSE TRUE 200000 TRUE 200001 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no costs order under rule 26.08`
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the unaccepted offer` `the defendant` FALSE TRUE 200000 TRUE 210000 15000 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the plaintiff's costs on the standard basis to 11 am on the second business day after service, and the defendant's costs on the standard basis after`
-- The plaintiff lost after unreasonably refusing the defendant's offer; and after a refusal not found unreasonable.
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the unaccepted offer` `the defendant` FALSE TRUE 200000 FALSE 0 0 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the defendant's costs on the standard basis to 11 am on the second business day after the offer, and on the indemnity basis after`
#ASSERT `What costs order follows the unaccepted offer` `the defendant` FALSE TRUE 200000 FALSE 0 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no costs order under rule 26.08`

-- Served Friday 13 November 2026: Tuesday 17 November; with a public holiday, Wednesday 18. Served Wednesday 11 November:
-- Friday 13 November.
#ASSERT `From when do the offer's costs consequences run` (`d` 13 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS `d` 17 11 2026
#ASSERT `From when do the offer's costs consequences run` (`d` 13 11 2026) TRUE EQUALS `d` 18 11 2026
#ASSERT `From when do the offer's costs consequences run` (`d` 11 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS `d` 13 11 2026

-- Arguments: in writing before the case, open a reasonable time, accepted, result no less favourable.
#ASSERT `Must the Court consider my pre-litigation offer` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the Court consider my pre-litigation offer` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Must the Court consider my pre-litigation offer` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Must the Court consider my pre-litigation offer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
